{"title":"Base Angle Theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Base Angle Theorem</b> states that in an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Isosceles_triangle\" title=\"Isosceles triangle\">isosceles triangle</a>, the angles opposite the congruent sides are congruent.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Proofs\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proofs</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Proof_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Proof_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Proof_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proofs\">Proofs</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Base_Angle_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proofs\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_1\">Proof 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Base_Angle_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Sines\" title=\"Law of Sines\">Law of Sines</a>, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c53914b18fc43acc37a27faa1ecf740c608c7564.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{b}{\\sin(B)}=\\tfrac{c}{\\sin(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"105\" height=\"24\" />. We know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/d/ebda5306c70a24c574ef0107ed5b5152b5f594cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=c$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/6/f6643e28e4fb3615abf81dacc54d4b516e39aaee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(B)=\\sin(C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />. Then either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/f/abf7026c16cd53bd4c951c73249436b4efcf0f78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94b4b9ec8f6a69faa533f55c5ce8aae81723e6de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=180-C$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"102\" height=\"13\" />, but the second case would imply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/4/8546e8a4097a0b4c1f6d1949aea75223232cc00a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=0^{\\circ}$\" width=\"53\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/f/abf7026c16cd53bd4c951c73249436b4efcf0f78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_2\">Proof 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Base_Angle_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Proof 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/d/d1d3d796b2121287048a85d7823d41496cd5a4de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB} \\cong \\overline{AC}$\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" /> (given). By the reflexive property, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/b/a3b2aec07adc601abec6815c32c4022a7e94023e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC} \\cong \\overline{CB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"19\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/13293eaf50f5ead8f06fb1d9ea53e7c53003059e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CA} \\cong \\overline{BA}$\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" /> (given).  By SSS, we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/e/61e7d5813625c92982234f8d2f1df767af676b62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta ABC \\cong \\Delta ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"142\" height=\"15\" />. By CPCTC, we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/98636815b33fd763aa9d12307ce064a0d45a9e75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC \\cong \\angle ACB$\" width=\"134\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_3\">Proof 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Base_Angle_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Proof 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the triangle only has three sides, the two congruent sides must be adjacent. Let them meet at vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Now we draw <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Altitude\" title=\"Altitude\">altitude</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. From the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/e/c2e6eb0f82cef23a536991757d354753feeaad5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=CD$\" width=\"84\" height=\"12\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/6/99652fb27a02d9cf4b12ff1935f5e4320fdb9fc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DBA=\\angle DCA$\" width=\"137\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/6/7f66cb51375e207e519d2fb8340d23232cff7953.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(5); defaultpen(fontsize(10)); pair A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H; A=(0,10); B=(-5,0); C=(5,0); D=(0,0); E=(1,1); F=(-1,1); G=(-1,0); H=(1,0); draw(A--B); draw(B--C); draw(C--A); draw(A--D); draw(E--F); draw(E--H); draw(F--G); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,S);[/asy]\" width=\"122\" height=\"122\" />\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Base_Angle_Theorem&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017234229\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.030 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 104/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 295/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3794/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.898      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.898      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7231:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017234229 and revision id 240398. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}